<section id="studio" aria-labelledby="studio-title" class="relative bg-bone px-[6vw] pb-28 pt-24 md:pb-40 md:pt-32"><div class="flex items-center gap-5"><p class="mono-label whitespace-nowrap">05<!-- --> — <!-- -->Studio</p><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px flex-1 bg-current opacity-20"></span></div><div class="mt-14 grid gap-16 md:mt-24 md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-10"><div class="md:col-span-5"><h2 id="studio-title" data-reveal="" class="font-heading text-[clamp(3rem,6vw,6.5rem)] leading-[0.9] tracking-[-0.02em]"><span class="reveal-line"><span style="transition-delay:0s">A small studio</span></span><span class="reveal-line"><span style="transition-delay:0.1s">with a <em class="italic">loud</em> kiln.</span></span></h2><p class="reveal-settle mt-10 max-w-md text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-charcoal/80" style="transition-delay:0.2s">Argjilë is the Albanian word for clay. Ours is a single room in Prishtina with two wheels under north-facing windows, a long glazing bench and a kiln that hums through the night. Everything is thrown, trimmed, glazed and fired here, in small batches, by the same four hands.</p><ul class="mt-14 border-t border-charcoal/15"><li class="border-b border-charcoal/15 py-5"><p class="font-mono text-[clamp(1.35rem,2.1vw,1.9rem)] tracking-[-0.01em]"><span class="tabular-nums">2019</span><span> — Founded</span></p></li><li class="border-b border-charcoal/15 py-5"><p class="font-mono text-[clamp(1.35rem,2.1vw,1.9rem)] tracking-[-0.01em]"><span class="tabular-nums">1</span><span> kiln, </span><span class="tabular-nums">2</span><span> wheels</span></p></li><li class="border-b border-charcoal/15 py-5"><p class="font-mono text-[clamp(1.35rem,2.1vw,1.9rem)] tracking-[-0.01em]"><span>~</span><span class="tabular-nums">400</span><span> pieces a year</span></p></li></ul></div><div class="reveal-settle md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7 md:pt-4" style="transition-delay:0s"><figure class="w-full"><div class="relative border border-charcoal/15 p-4 md:p-6" style="